    "result": "Fixed the bug in `sqlparse/engine/statement_splitter.py:74-77`: the `END` handler had an inverted condition (`if not (self._block_stack): self._block_stack.pop()`), which popped from an empty list whenever a bare `END` appeared with no open block — exactly what happens when a `CASE ... END` is inside a plain `SELECT` statement (no `BEGIN` context). Corrected it to pop only `if self._block_stack:`, matching the pattern used by the other closing-keyword branches."
  },
